WEBVTT

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.910
I'm still surprised that we chose the place
the Golden Ghost Ship appeared for the battle.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.450
No dark clouds here now.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.660
No debris. No anything.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.670
It's all clear.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.710
The perfect setting for a battle.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.920
Hotline!

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:32.880
Chiaki!

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.840
What's up?

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:52.780
I believe...

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.110
...in you, and in our future.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.200
Touchdown in front of us.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.620
Three ships of all the same type!

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.580
Three Grand Crosses?

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.520
Are you serious?!

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.850
Chiaki, leave it to me.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.510
Is everyone ready?

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.010
Ready!

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.440
Now, let's get going.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.890
Go get 'em!

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.340
Within enemy firing range!

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.360
That's okay!

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.680
Take us just within firing range!

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.430
On the EW front, we're even.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.140
They've linked ships and are working in union.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.170
Not bad.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.600
But even working together,

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.100
you are no match for the Grand Cross.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:03.900
Ruthless!

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.290
Don't worry.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:06.410
Our jamming is holding.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:10.550
For now, the Bentenmaru will focus on ECM.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.050
Keep an eye out for gravity wave signals.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.460
Got it!

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:19.020
I have faith in the experience that a pirate has.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.170
I'm betting on all the experience this ship has collected.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:30.180
Because I'm a pirate...

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.430
Because I'm a pirate!

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:40.940
Bentenmaru, take us around to their right, just at the edge of their firing radius.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.440
Roger.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.210
Amazing.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.390
We can clearly see where our enemies and allies are,

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:07.840
and we can predict their positions five minutes out.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.300
This way, no one will be stupid enough to fire on an ally.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.310
Gravity Wave Signal

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:18.640
Gravity Waves?

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:24.650
There it is!

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.610
Gravity wave signals rising.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.280
Here comes the zigzag!

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.990
I have its pattern down.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.410
It isn't perfect, but pay attention, students.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.220
Got it!

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:38.750
Okay.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.760
She's coming for the El Santo?

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:48.170
Bring it.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.640
Is she guiding all three ships herself?

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:58.730
Herself?

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.240
I get it.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.490
That would make sense.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:03.610
It would?

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.280
They're moving randomly, but all three are really moving on a single plane.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.490
It's like a board game.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.490
She seemed like someone who doesn't enjoy losing.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.210
What a futile struggle.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.500
I shall begin with one ship.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.410
I see.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.820
Overwhelming.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.690
But that gives us plenty of opportunities.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.540
Self-destruct?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.090
A decoy?

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:04.790
No!

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.480
Missile strike on the chaff field!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.360
She was kind enough to come and play.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.860
Let's give her a warm welcome.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.870
Allied positions confirmed.

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.970
We've got a great view of the battlefield.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:47.220
The Bentenmaru girl's pretty smart!

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:50.800
Enemy ship en route to aid the one that's under fire.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.560
Okay!

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.390
Low of War, move to intercept!

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.430
Love Machine will assist the Low of War.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.780
Don't forget me!

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.390
Okay, come on!

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:10.490
The gravity wave shield is only
effective against beam weapons.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:16.580
It won't last long against physical projectiles, such as missiles, especially in a wide-area attack like this.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:21.240
And of course, pirate missiles are ruthless too.

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.920
All right, that's one down!

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.380
We are the Original Eight!

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:29.970
Nine.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:30.880
Ten.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.640
Pirates acting like a fleet, huh?

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:45.650
It's kind of strange.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.190
They used to do it, right?

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:49.830
During the war of independence though.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.440
But this is probably the first time in a hundred years.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.210
Everyone's doing a great job.

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:56.780
We're like a real fleet!

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:04.580
Well, a fleet's just a bunch of guys always doing weapon tests and military exercises.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:06.750
So are we.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:12.670
If you can't work with someone
right away, you can't do this job.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.980
Any sign of enemy reinforcements?

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.060
Nope.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:17.840
Okay!

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.900
Captain, message from the Shangri-La.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.180
They say they're ready whenever.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:26.860
Got it.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.950
Misa, take care of the rest.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:30.400
Schnitzer, Hyakume.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:31.620
Right.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.200
Good luck, Coorie.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.580
All right.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.160
You're really doing this?

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:37.400
Of course.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.160
Now it's our turn to board her.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:43.740
If we let her grab more glory, we aren't pirates.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.410
You get that from your mother.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.260
How uninspiring.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.680
I'll simply exit the chaff!

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:26.450
You pushed forward too far, Miss.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:34.210
Now eat your fill.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.440
Second ship neutralized.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:47.220
The rest is up to you, Captain Marika!

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:00.250
The Bentenmaru...

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.570
Kato Marika!

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.170
Enemy has targeted the Bentenmaru!

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:22.480
Kane.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:23.300
I'm on it.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:28.530
I guess your brother did well during the last battle.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:30.680
I'm better than my brother.

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.810
All right, just watch.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:41.320
Kato Marika!

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:44.450
I can't see anything.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:57.420
What happened?

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:02.060
They can't be...

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:03.130
They're boarding?

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:15.350
Yup.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.860
Is everyone ready?

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:23.860
It's time for some piracy!

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:52.810
Chiaki.

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:59.150
After this battle, what will you do?

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.280
I like my job.

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:06.780
This fight is for my pride as well.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:11.750
But I'm sure not everyone sees it the same way.

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.160
What do you want to do?

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:18.790
Will you go with Captain Marika?

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:29.990
Attack!

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:36.850
What?

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:40.520
That's...

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.030
Captain Sumi Kuki of the Murakamimaru!

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.630
Amazing.

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:58.050
Not only because he's a pirate.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:14:59.290
He's just amazing!

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:04.290
Okay, it's just as we thought.

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:06.470
Everything is basically automatic.

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:09.060
She's piloting alone.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.060
And our goal is...

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:11.880
Is where?

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.080
Quartz!

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.770
Quartz Christie!

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:28.940
Welcome, Marika.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:48.510
Welcome to the Grand Cross.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.900
I thought it'd be deserted.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:54.010
Thanks for coming to see me.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.470
I won't run or hide.

00:15:57.650 --> 00:15:59.020
That said...

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:02.700
You really are flashy.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.020
I'm a pirate, so of course.

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:08.190
I wanted to continue our discussion.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:09.530
Continue?

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.460
About how we're not pirates anymore.

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:15.380
All we do is put on little shows. We're unneeded.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.410
You said that, right?

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.660
Yes.

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:21.470
Sure, I wonder about the performances.

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:23.640
Sometimes, we get a little too into it.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:24.670
Even still...

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:29.770
I'm here now.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.560
Kato Marika, captain of the Bentenmaru, exists here.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.150
At this point in time and space.

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.560
Why am I a pirate?

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.930
Because I am Kato Marika!

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.190
Is that not an answer?

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:48.940
That's because there isn't a question.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:50.440
So we're even.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:52.690
Even?

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.250
Raise your hands, and come this way.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.620
We will treat prisoners in accordance with Stellar Military law.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.340
Oh, no!

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:13.480
Run.

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:15.010
This ship will self-destruct soon.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:19.820
I suspected as much.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:21.720
Captain, there's no point in staying.

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:27.560
Marika?

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.230
What?

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.730
Come to a vaster sea.

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:34.780
There is someone who desires that.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:45.960
This is the end of the Grand Cross.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:55.170
In the clear night and the silence of time,

00:17:56.050 --> 00:18:05.100
